# Recorded fingerprints, for telling a refactor from a regression.
#
# Nothing in here is committed except this file. A fingerprint is a property of
# the toolchain that produced it as much as of the code: it shifts in the last
# digits with the compiler, the BLAS implementation and, when
# BAYESTS_NATIVE_ARCH is on, the CPU. A baseline checked in here would therefore
# fail on every machine except the one that recorded it, which is why the test
# suite compares a before against an after on one machine instead of comparing
# against a stored expectation.
#
# The directory is tracked -- rather than left to be created by hand -- so that
# `ctest ... -R golden -V > test/baselines/<name>.txt` works in a fresh clone
# and lands somewhere that survives `rm -rf build`.
#
# Date the files, or name them for the change they precede. A baseline recorded
# before a build-flag change is worse than no baseline at all: it still diffs
# cleanly enough to look meaningful.
*
!.gitignore
